  "summary": "Beautiful white sand beach with unique rock formations and clear turquoise waters in Jember, East Java",
  "description": "Papuma Beach, located in Jember Regency of East Java, is renowned for its stunning white sand and crystal-clear turquoise waters. The name 'Papuma' is an acronym from 'Pasir Putih Malikan' which means Malikan's White Sand. The beach features unique rock formations scattered along the coastline and offers panoramic views from nearby hilltops.\r\n\r\nUnlike many other beaches in East Java, Papuma boasts fine white sand and relatively calm waters during the dry season. The beach is surrounded by lush green hills and features several small islands that can be reached during low tide. While swimming is limited due to strong Indian Ocean currents, the beach offers excellent opportunities for photography, relaxation, and enjoying spectacular sunsets.\r\n\r\nThe combination of white sand, turquoise waters, and unique geological formations makes Papuma one of East Java's most picturesque coastal destinations.",
  "highlight": "White sand beach with turquoise waters and unique rock formations. Cape headland Tanjung Papuma ~86m. The only coastal stop on a JVTO East Java circuit — between Ijen night hike and Tumpak Sewu canyon descent.",
