  "cultural_context": "Papuma Beach holds significance as one of the few white sand beaches in East Java's southern coast. The name 'Papuma' comes from 'Pasir Putih Malikan' (Malikan's White Sand), reflecting local pride in this natural treasure. While less steeped in ancient traditions than volcanic sites, the beach represents the element of Water in local cosmology and serves as an important recreational space for local communities.",
